# NOT NEEDED for `npm run mockup`: it keeps the Datasource + Storage of the mockup on THIS machine (.mockup-data/, git-ignored) — no server, no token.
# Copy this file to .env.mockup.local (git-ignored) only to use a shared file server on purpose; `npm run mockup -- --local` still keeps the data local.
# MOCKUP_REMOTE_URL=<the address of the shared file server, https://…>
# the shared secret of that server: ask whoever runs it
# MOCKUP_TOKEN=
# MOCKUP_WORKSPACE=<your name>   OPTIONAL with a shared server. Leave it out and you share the ONE state with everybody. Set it to try things
#                                 without touching the data of the others: what you write goes to Datasource/_workspaces/<name>/ on the server and only you see it.
# MOCKUP_REMOTE_IP=<IPv4>        OPTIONAL: the address to connect to instead of looking the domain up (the name stays in https + Host).
